tcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BbzjDVihXN58pwsEEmfb6t", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["honor_retry_after", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380102, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BbzjDVihXN58pwsEEmfb6t", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383545, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up, although its own description says it should use banker's rounding (round half to even) per FIN-212. So `2.665` came out as `2.68`, but `tests/test_money.py` expects `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TuAWni5zC7dZQq46zRzFDk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01452nDfcKHbMbALSRsya4is", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LZT1qB2b5DteiJYGrckveJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Kr6G3eF1jV1vKgoyTWFu5x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QB7Av2pR6NzbTYVi3eq7bP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SHD1o4jT4zC7jXzjA1VkJ5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WdhiEocYaazyTBNJQVr1XH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BbzjDVihXN58pwsEEmfb6t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` say it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), per FIN-212.\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. With that change, `Decimal(\"2.665\")` rounds to `2.66` and `2.675` rounds to `2.68`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up, although its own description says it should use banker's rounding (round half to even) per FIN-212. So `2.665` came out as `2.68`, but `tests/test_money.py` expects `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}